# The build context for every service image is the repository root, because
# Directory.Build.props, Directory.Build.targets, Directory.Packages.props, global.json,
# .editorconfig and the AgenticShop.Shared ProjectReference all live there. Without this file
# the daemon is sent the whole repository on every build.
#
# bin/ and obj/ are excluded for correctness, not only for speed: an obj/project.assets.json
# written by a restore on Windows records host paths, and copying it into a Linux build layer
# hands the in-container restore assets that do not describe it.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.qwen/

# Not read by the Dockerfile. Excluded so the context stays small and the build cache stays
# usable — a documentation edit should not invalidate a layer.
docs/
tests/
http/
scripts/
docker/postgres/
docker-compose.yml
**/*.md
.env
.env.example

# Kept, and load-bearing: .editorconfig drives the style diagnostics that TreatWarningsAsErrors
# turns into build failures, so a build without it enforces a different rule set than the host.
!.editorconfig
